Let me re-verify. Dolly the sheep is widely documented as being born on 5 July 1996 at the Roslin Institute in Scotland. The cloning was achieved using nuclear transfer of an adult somatic (mammary gland) cell, and her existence was announced to the public in February 1997, which is likely the source of my earlier confusion between the birth date and the announcement date.

My earlier answer of 1997 was incorrect — that was the year of the public announcement, not the year of her birth. Also, I mistakenly mentioned a Nobel Prize awarded in 2003 related to the team, which is inaccurate; no Nobel Prize was awarded for Dolly's cloning.

