Let me verify. The 1866 transatlantic cable was laid by the *Great Eastern*, Isambard Kingdom Brunel's massive ship, which was the largest vessel in the world at the time. It was chartered by the Telegraph Construction and Maintenance Company and successfully laid the cable from Valentia Island, Ireland, to Heart's Content, Newfoundland, in 1866. It also recovered and completed the broken 1865 cable that same year.

My earlier answer said "Great Western" — but the *Great Western* was an earlier Brunel steamship (1837), a passenger liner that was never a cable layer. I confused the two similar names. The correct ship is the *Great Eastern*.

